Controller AuditLog integration tests
-------------------------------------
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.readEntryLogsRealReadAction - read writes a real READ row
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.addEntryLogsRealCreateAction - add writes a real CREATE row
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.reviewAuditLogShowsRealEntries - review shows the logged rows
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.readEntrySkipsAuditWhenUserUnknown - no log row when the user is unknown
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.reviewAuditLogRejectsStandardUser - standard user cannot review the audit log
ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest.readEntryNotFoundLogsNothing - not-found read writes no row
Notes: real AuditLog over a real SQLiteDataStore on a test
database behind the full Controller; users, access, and
messages stay mocked. The acting user is seeded into the
store first, since log rows reference their user.
The Controller is constructed with a mocked
SessionManager as its 6th argument.
Run: .\gradlew test --tests "control.ControllerAuditLogIntegrationTest" --console=plain
